<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- Biotech role traits (loaded only with Biotech). Puppet master evolves with the mechs overseen ("Puppetry", mech-days). -->
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>CVG_Role_PuppetMaster</defName>
    <commonality>0.04</commonality>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>CVG_Role</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <forcedPassions>
      <li>Crafting</li>
    </forcedPassions>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <label>apprentice puppet master</label>
        <description>Bonds with puppets of metal and qi come naturally: if {PAWN_nameDef} is a mechanitor, {PAWN_pronoun} gains extra bandwidth. Improves by overseeing mechs. The puppeteers of Jiuxiao carved wooden warriors long before the Iron Calamity showed them what metal could do.</description>
        <commonality>1</commonality>
        <skillGains>
          <Crafting>3</Crafting>
        </skillGains>
        <statOffsets>
          <MechBandwidth>1</MechBandwidth>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
      <li>
        <degree>1</degree>
        <label>puppet master</label>
        <labelFemale>puppet master</labelFemale>
        <description>Commands puppets of metal and qi with ease: as a mechanitor, {PAWN_nameDef} gains more bandwidth and an extra control group. Improves by overseeing mechs. After the Calamity some sects swore never to animate metal again; only the puppeteers kept the art alive.</description>
        <commonality>0.15</commonality>
        <skillGains>
          <Crafting>5</Crafting>
        </skillGains>
        <statOffsets>
          <MechBandwidth>2</MechBandwidth>
          <MechControlGroups>1</MechControlGroups>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
      <li>
        <degree>2</degree>
        <label>grandmaster of puppets</label>
        <labelFemale>grandmaster of puppets</labelFemale>
        <description>A whole army of puppets moves as one body: as a mechanitor, {PAWN_nameDef} has the widest bandwidth and an extra control group. Legend says the last puppet grandmaster of Jiuxiao turned the Iron Calamity's own husks against it.</description>
        <commonality>0.02</commonality>
        <skillGains>
          <Crafting>7</Crafting>
        </skillGains>
        <statOffsets>
          <MechBandwidth>3</MechBandwidth>
          <MechControlGroups>1</MechControlGroups>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.DefModExtension_TraitProgression">
        <counter>Puppetry</counter>
        <steps>
          <li>
            <degree>1</degree>
            <threshold>30</threshold>
          </li>
          <li>
            <degree>2</degree>
            <threshold>120</threshold>
          </li>
        </steps>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </TraitDef>
  <TraitDef>
    <defName>CVG_Role_BloodChild</defName>
    <commonality>0.03</commonality>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>CVG_Role</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>CVG_Heart_Buddha</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <label>child of blood</label>
        <labelFemale>child of blood</labelFemale>
        <description>Blood calls to {PAWN_nameDef}: hemogen comes easily and wounds close fast. The blood path was opened by Chiyou's war-shamans long before the Blood Moon Cult claimed it, and its echo has beaten in these veins since birth.</description>
        <skillGains>
          <Melee>2</Melee>
        </skillGains>
        <statFactors>
          <HemogenGainFactor>1.25</HemogenGainFactor>
          <InjuryHealingFactor>1.15</InjuryHealingFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="Convergence.DefModExtension_TraitConflicts">
        <conflicts>
          <li><trait>Immunity</trait><degree>-1</degree></li>
          <li><trait>Delicate</trait></li>
          <li><trait>Wimp</trait></li>
        </conflicts>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </TraitDef>
</Defs>
